# Development Workflow Rule

Never start coding directly from a user request without first classifying size and risk.

Required workflow:

User Request
→ Project Memory depth by size
→ Skill Selection Gate
→ Size Classification Gate (XS / S / M / L)
→ Multi-Expert Subagent Gate when size/risk requires it
→ GitHub Reference Gate only when no existing skill/rule fits
→ Size-specific documents
→ Single / Parallel Task Execution according to Context Pack
→ Integration Review when risk or subagents justify it
→ Tests / verification
→ Evidence / Acceptance according to size
→ Changelog / Memory Update according to size
→ Retrospective / Skill Extraction only when useful or required

Size-specific documents:

- XS: no pre-implementation docs; final response records files, verification, and residual risk.
- S: one TASK with embedded Context Pack, Evidence, and Acceptance.
- M: SPEC + TASK + Context Pack by default; add REQ, PLAN, or PRD only when triggered.
- L: full PRD / REQ / SPEC / PLAN / TASK / Context Pack.

Upgrade XS/S when API, DB, dependency, security, Agent/RAG, model-provider, deployment, or frontend/backend contract risk appears.
